  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Sucrose hydrolyses in acid solution into glucose and fructose following first order rate law with a half-life of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>33</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;After <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;the fraction of sucrose remaining is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi></mfrac></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is ________&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;(Rounded off to the nearest integer)</p><p>[Assume: In<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>303</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>693</mn></math>]</p>"
  },
